course: dictionary
lesson: 14115
title: Methodism: a church movement
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: Some words name a whole group of people and what they believe. Methodism is one of them. It is a Christian church movement: a large group of people who share the same beliefs and ways of worship. It names a thing, so it is a noun, and it has no plural.
explain: Look at the clues around it. «John Wesley started Methodism in England.» The words started and England tell you that it began as a movement, in England, with people who led it. «Methodists sing hymns and read the Bible together.» Methodists are the people who follow Methodism. The word looks like Methodism with an extra ending that makes a person.
explain: Swap your meaning into the sentence to check it. «Methodism helps the poor and is known for warm preaching.» Put in "a church movement" instead: "A church movement helps the poor and is known for warm preaching" still makes sense, so your idea is right. If a word like Protestant is hard, skip it, read on, and come back later.
fact: Methodism is a Christian Protestant church movement.
fact: Methodism was started by John and Charles Wesley in England.
fact: Methodism is known for warm preaching, hymn singing, Bible study and helping the poor.
fact: Methodism spread among working people in towns and mining villages, and to America.
fact: Methodists meet in chapels or churches, and Charles Wesley wrote many hymns that are still sung today.
exercise: «John Wesley started Methodism in England.» Where did Methodism begin? | France | *England | Italy | Scotland
exercise: «Methodists sing hymns and read the Bible together.» What do Methodists do together? | *Sing hymns and study the Bible | Paint pictures | Build ships | Race horses
exercise: Who wrote many hymns that are still sung today? | *Charles Wesley | Florence Nightingale | Queen Victoria | Captain Cook
test: «Methodism grew among working people in towns and mining villages.» Where did Methodism grow? | Desert camps | Royal palaces | Ocean islands | *Towns and mining villages
test: Which word is the name of the movement itself? | Methodist | Methodical | Method | *Methodism
exam: Which is NOT one of the things Methodism is known for? | *Building castles | Hymn singing | Bible study | Warm preaching
